+# Task Tracker UI Acceptance Evidence
+
+## Source
+
+- Source commit: `7b4320718687825ec229c01853242f0c81050ad7`.
+- Baseline: `569c1b9249aed1d552a5d3444c92f73dde94691d`, branch
+  `feat/base-ui-standard`, isolated worktree `.local/uiux-standard-workspace/task-tracker`.
+- Base commit: `2a8de7ed2e4e7475bfcfb80e87222af4cc1fbc93`.
+- Installed/source Base fingerprint:
+  `44f46615a419570df8e12a7968a3aebd4124c3157c5da095b61e55dcbfa8a744`.
+- Product fingerprint:
+  `72a8069d5120d813a86f6c319005ca66cfcf19dc9e0de132a49d4da71866d4e9`.
+- Image digest, launcher acceptance, live SSO, full backend gate: `not-run`.
+  This is source QA, not release acceptance. Route manifest remains `pending`.
+
+## Gates
+
+Evidence root: `audit-artifacts/base-standard-2026-10-01/` in the SDLC workspace.
+
+| Command | Exit | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| `pnpm install --offline --frozen-lockfile` | 0 | `task-base-final-install.log`; lockfile unchanged |
+| `pnpm test` | 0 | `task-base-final-units.log`; 46 files, 274 tests |
+| `pnpm lint` | 0 | `task-base-final-lint.log`; ESLint and semantic check |
+| `pnpm build` | 0 | `task-base-final-build.log`; typecheck and Vite build |
+| `pnpm ui:check` | 0 | 16 patterns, installed/source bytes match; runtime still required |
+| Base gate `--fingerprint` | 0 | fingerprints above |
+| Chromium `e2e/smoke.spec.ts`, one worker | 0 | `task-base-final-browser.log`; 3 tests, 3.5 minutes |
+| `git diff --check` | 0 | reviewed source delta before commit |
+
+## Browser Matrix
+
+Final build, mocked API/OIDC, `localhost:18865`. Playwright-owned preview was
+stopped after the terminal result; the port had no listener afterward.
+
+- 120 full-page captures: dashboard/projects/create/detail x gray/dark/light x
+  375/767/768/1023/1024/1279/1280/1440/1920/2560 px.
+- Checked layout modes, frame widths, 760 px reading limit, header height 60 px,
+  sidebar 264/72 px or hidden, one Base shell/header and nonoverlapping header
+  slots, no document overflow, detail aside 320 px above 1024.
+- Visible main buttons/selects/inputs/textareas measured at minimum 40 desktop /
+  44 mobile. Hidden fields, file inputs and checkbox/radio graphics excluded.
+- Unknown URL preserves query through mocked SSO and reload; not-found remains
+  inside protected wide shell. Drawer opens by keyboard, retains focus inside,
+  Escape closes and returns focus; destination links are not duplicated.
+- Dirty summary survives query tabs, Back, seven resize widths and cancelled
+  navigation. Failed PATCH preserves draft and shows an error; one submission
+  observed. Delete cancellation returns focus to its actions button.
+- Separate unit fixtures cover cached 403/404 hiding and dependent read disabling,
+  cached 503 partial/retry, independent dashboard errors and custom field refetch.
+- Final desktop dashboard/detail and mobile detail captures inspected visually.
+  An extra `draft-save-failure.png` records the controlled save failure.
+
+Artifacts: [final browser captures](../../../../audit-artifacts/base-standard-2026-10-01/task-base-final-browser/),
+[final browser log](../../../../audit-artifacts/base-standard-2026-10-01/task-base-final-browser.log).
+The earlier `task-base-source-browser` run predates the final Base Select migration
+and is not evidence for the final controls.
+
+This matrix does not cover every manifest pattern, normal reload per pattern,
+all roles, complete loading/empty/error/403/404/partial fixtures, or all console
+and network assertions. Those remain required release work, not inferred passes.
+Local FORCE_COLOR/NO_COLOR warnings are retained in the log.
+
+## Gallery
+
+README gallery was not regenerated from mocks. Current gallery provenance and
+real desktop captures remain release backlog. Mocked smoke cannot write README
+images via the former `UPDATE_README_SCREENSHOTS` switch.
+
+## Release
+
+No GitHub/fetch/Actions, push, default integration, mirror sync or runtime pin
+changes in this checkpoint. The original dirty checkout was not edited.
+See [Remaining Acceptance](UI_UX_MAP.md#remaining-acceptance).
